WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.600
From 1994, Cheap Diclofenac cut India's vultures to 1,000th and added over 100,000 deaths yearly. This is unintended consequences, episode 151. A pain killer meant for working cattle, a scavenger collapsed, nobody measured, a sanitation gap that reached people, a band that leaked, and the test that was never required. Diclofenac began as a human drug. In the 1970s, it was developed as a non-steroidal anti-inflammatory for arthritis.

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:35.960
and for pain after surgery. It did what that class of drugs is built to do. It eased swelling,

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:42.600
it gave people back ordinary movement. When the patent lapsed in the early 1990s, Indian pharmaceutical

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:49.120
firms made inexpensive versions. Farmers could finally afford a dose. Before that shift, livestock

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:54.760
owners had few practical options for the pain and inflammation that cut milk yields and draft

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:59.980
power in working animals. A bullock that could not plow was not only an animal in distress,

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:05.100
it was a season of field work at risk. The drug therefore looked like a straightforward

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:10.580
welfare gain and a productivity gain for millions of small holders who had watched cattle suffer

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:15.500
without treatment. No one at the time tested the compound on the obligate scavengers

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:23.540
that cleaned the countryside of dead livestock. That omission was not a secret plot. It was

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:29.160
any published data on avian kidney physiology, the decision carried no visible downside for

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:31.540
the people who made the drug or administered it.

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:37.780
Farmers in the Genetic Plane and in Rajasthan, where cattle densities were highest, saw immediate

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:41.580
improvements in animal mobility after a single low-cost injection.

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:46.580
The same dose that ease joint swelling in a bullock also kept the animal productive for

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:48.580
another season of plowing or hauling.

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:53.940
Because Diclofenak was already approved for human use, regulators treated the extension

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:58.680
to livestock as a minor administrative step, rather than a new environmental release.

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:01.540
The economic logic was simple arithmetic.

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:06.500
One vile treated several animals at a fraction of the price of imported alternatives.

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:10.780
Milk output or field work could resume within days instead of weeks.

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:16.160
For a smallholder counting days until the next milking or the next planting, that arithmetic

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:17.580
was hard to argue with.

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:19.580
The intended patient was the cow.

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:22.160
The intended return was work and milk.

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:26.060
Both of those showed up quickly, and both of those were easy to see.

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:31.520
By the mid-1990s, veterinary use had spread rapidly through the cattle belt of northern

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:32.660
and western India.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:38.260
Roadside pharmacies and livestock markets stocked the human formulation in vials labelled

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:38.760
for cattle.

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:43.140
Farmers injected animals shortly before slaughter or natural death.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:48.940
Early surveys by the Bombay Natural History Society recorded no obvious change in carcass

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:49.480
availability.

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:53.480
Vultures still arrived in large numbers at known feeding sites.

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:58.120
If you were standing at one of those sites in those years, the old picture still held.

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:00.380
Birds came, carcasses went.

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:05.860
A few ornithologist noted occasional dead birds with white urate deposits around the vent.

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:10.880
Those incidents were treated as isolated disease events rather than a systemic threat.

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:14.260
But that reading was available from the evidence then in hand.

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:19.480
A handful of dead birds against flocks that still filled the sky did not yet look like

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:19.920
a collapse.

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:23.780
The scale of adoption can be traced in pharmacy sales records.

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:29.180
Once the molecule entered the generic market, annual production volumes rose from laboratory

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:31.040
quantities to hundreds of tons.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:36.140
That was enough to dose millions of cattle each year across states where open grazing was

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:36.560
the norm.

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:36.660
firm.

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:42.260
Because the human and veterinary supply chains were not yet separated by regulation, the

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:47.180
same blister packs moved from urban hospitals to rural veterinary shops with minimal friction.

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:52.860
A drug approved for people did not have to change plants or packaging logic, or much of

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:54.160
its root to reach a bullock.

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:58.680
Early monitoring focused on whether the drug reduced clinical signs in livestock.

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:04.080
No parallel program tracked residue levels in the carcasses those livestock left behind.

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:09.380
The first systematic necropsies that later linked the drug to vulture mortality were still

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:14.260
years away, so the absence of reported problems was taken as evidence of safety.

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:17.100
Silence in the data was read as a clean result.

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:21.420
It was, more precisely, a result no one had yet gone looking for.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:26.260
The causal chain began when a treated animal died, and its carcass retained enough

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:29.340
dichlofenac residue to kill any vulture that fed on it.

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:31.920
The bird did not have to receive an injection.

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:34.640
It only had to do the work it had always done.

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:40.540
In 2004, Jay Lindsay Oaks and colleagues published in Nature the experimental proof.

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:45.740
Oral doses matching those found in treated livestock produced the visceral gout and kidney

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:48.020
failure already seen in field carcasses.

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:53.120
The white deposits ornithologists had noted years earlier were not a scattered disease.

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:55.260
They were a signature of the drug.

00:04:55.260 --> 00:05:01.160
By 2007, the Oriental Whitebacked Vulture had declined to one-tenth of one percent of its

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:07.280
early 1990s numbers, according to repeated road transect surveys reported in PLOS-1.

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:15.220
A 97% drop recorded between the early 1990s and 2007 left two few birds to process the daily

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:18.320
volume of livestock mortality across the subcontinent.

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:24.080
Three-jip species that had once numbered in the tens of millions were, within a decade of the

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:29.320
generic flood, a remnant. The arithmetic of exposure is straightforward once the residue

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:34.400
data are examined. A single-treated buffalo could contain several lethal doses for a

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:40.460
vulture. Gip species feed in groups of dozens. One contaminated carcass could remove multiple

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:45.480
breeding adults in a single afternoon. Without those adults returning to nests, recruitment

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:50.820
collapsed. The loss was not only of birds in the air, it was of the next generation that

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:55.660
those birds would have raised. With the primary scavengers gone, the carcasses that once

00:05:55.660 --> 00:06:00.100
disappeared within hours lay rotting for days at village dumps and urban waste sites.

00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:04.140
That persistence was the first visible rearrangement of the countryside.

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:10.100
Feral dog populations rose sharply because an abundant, previously contested food source

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:15.880
was now uncontested. Each additional dog raised the probability of a human bite. India

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:20.720
India already accounted for roughly a third of global rabies deaths, so the bite risk landed

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:23.960
on a country that was already carrying a heavy share of that disease.

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:29.320
At the same time, uneaten carcasses leached pathogens into shallow aquifers and streams

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:30.900
used for washing and irrigation.

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:35.280
Surface water near carcass dumps showed elevated bacterial loads.

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:40.020
The effect concentrated in the same districts that had once supported the dense's vulture

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:40.500
colonies.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:46.540
The sanitation gap therefore ran through two measurable pathways, more dogs and dirtier

00:06:46.540 --> 00:06:49.300
water in the places where the birds had been thickest.

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:55.440
Economists Yael Frank and Anant Sudarshan used the natural experiment of districts that

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:58.220
historically differed in Vulture habitat suitability.

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:05.180
In the American Economic Review, they estimated that all cause human mortality rose 4.7% in

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:09.060
high suitability districts between 2000 and 2005.

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:14.120
Districts that had supported the largest vulture populations recorded human death rates

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:19.320
more than 4% higher than comparable districts that had never hosted many vultures.

00:07:19.780 --> 00:07:26.040
The 4.7% increase reflects both direct zoonotic risk and the broader degradation of local

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:29.420
water quality once the Keystone scavenger was removed.

00:07:29.940 --> 00:07:38.140
A narrow approval for a cattle pain killer had, through residue, kidney failure, and an

00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:44.240
India banned veterinary dichlofenac in 2006 and strengthened the prohibition in 2008.

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:49.980
The response was real, it was also late relative to the collapse already measured, and it

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:52.580
had to work through supply chains that had already mixed.

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:58.660
Follow-up Karkas surveys published in Pilos 1 showed the prevalence of dichlofenac contaminated

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:04.980
livestock fell from roughly 10.8% before the ban to 6.5% several years later.

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:07.180
That fall slowed the declines.

00:08:07.180 --> 00:08:08.760
It did not stop them.

00:08:09.140 --> 00:08:15.680
Necropses of vultures found dead between 2008 and 2012, reported in Oryx, revealed that

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:17.720
some birds still carried Diclophonac.

00:08:18.280 --> 00:08:22.440
Others showed nemisolide residues associated with the same gout pathology.

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:27.400
Human formulation Diclophonac continues to be diverted into veterinary channels.

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:33.500
Populations of the three-jip species remain at a few percent of pre-1990s levels, with

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:35.080
only modest signs of recovery.

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:40.060
The persistence of the drug after the formal ban illustrates the difficulty of separating

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:45.340
two parallel supply chains that share the same molecule and the same manufacturing plants.

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:51.600
Even after the 2008 tightening, which required colored dyes and larger vial sizes for human

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:55.720
formulations, enforcement relied on state-level pharmacy inspections.

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:59.260
Those inspections could not monitor every rural transaction.

00:08:59.960 --> 00:09:01.920
A dye and a bigger vial are signals.

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:08.480
cells. They are not a seal on every roadside shop. Meanwhile, alternative non-steroidal anti-inflammatory

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:13.440
drugs, such as Nemesolide, entered the veterinary market without the same level of pre-release

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:18.560
testing against vulture kidney tissue. The original oversight was reproduced at a smaller

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:23.800
scale. The band changed the label. It did not, by itself, change the question regulators

00:09:23.800 --> 00:09:30.260
had failed to ask in 1994. When regulators approved Dichlofenak for livestock, they evaluated

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:34.240
only the intended patient species and the immediate economic return to

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:39.000
farmers. The process rewarded any low-cost drug that cleared livestock quickly.

00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:43.280
It did not require tests on the scavengers whose removal would later impose

00:09:43.280 --> 00:09:47.960
sanitation costs in human lives. A second principle sits beside that one.

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:52.940
Once a compound enters widespread agricultural use, a later ban on the

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:56.280
veterinary formulation can still be undermined by leakage from the

00:09:56.280 --> 00:10:00.220
parallel human supply chain that regulators continue to authorize.

00:10:00.560 --> 00:10:05.000
The burden that was missing is a demonstration of safety for the entire local scavenger

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:06.820
community before marketing approval.

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:11.760
That requirement would move the proof from post-release mortality counts to pre-release

00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:12.440
feeding trials.

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:17.760
If you follow how an ecological loss shows up inside human death rates, environmental

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:21.040
intelligence on the Narin network stays with that kind of measurement.

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:27.420
The same narrow gate still opens whenever a livestock medicine is cleared on how fast a herd returns to work.

00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:35.240
If a new anti-inflammatory or antibiotic is approved for cattle on productivity data alone, what would you look for in the file,

00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:40.300
a feeding trial on the animals that eat the dead, or only a note that the cow stood up sooner?

00:10:40.920 --> 00:10:45.020
That's the case for today. The lessons tend to travel further when you share them,

00:10:45.180 --> 00:10:49.480
so send this one to someone who'd find it useful, and subscribe wherever you're listening.

